# Git Commit Rules

## Format

Always use conventional commits format:
`<type>: <short description>`

## Types

- `feat:` — new component or feature
- `fix:` — bug fix
- `style:` — CSS, styling changes, no logic change
- `refactor:` — code restructure without behavior change
- `chore:` — config, dependencies, project setup
- `docs:` — README, plan.md, comments

## Examples

- `feat: add hero section component`
- `style: update button hover color`
- `fix: correct navbar padding on mobile`
- `refactor: extract useReveal into custom hook`
- `chore: install lucide-react`
- `docs: update plan.md progress checklist`

## Rules

- Always lowercase
- No period at the end
- Max 72 characters
- Description in English
